let's do this  sonic the hedgehog spun his way onto the  silver screen releasing two very  successful blockbusters pleasing young  and old fans alike but who's voicing  these characters to success we're taking  you down a quick path of all the voices  and characters of the sonic the hedgehog  films  number one we think if anything's got to  be done right in a live action sonic  film it's got to be his personality and  who else better than ben schwartz to  take on the title character he's no  stranger to voice acting with a slew of  animated appearances his first being  disney's turbo as skidmark but once the  blue hedgehog landed in his repertoire  he was excited to give fans what they  wanted it's so fun to dive into the  mythology and to give the fans more of  what they want in terms of physical  movement he had an easier time than most  of the cast just keeping his voice in  tip-top shape number two who wasn't  excited for calling o'shaughnessy to  return to the classic role of tales we  certainly were it is an honor to finally  meet you sonic her impressive voice  acting resume extends from anime to  classic video game franchises top  credits go towards her work as the voice  of tales from the video games instantly  gaining approval from the die hard  fanbase with such a large attachment to  the character it was no surprise that  director jeff fowler wanted her to play  the titular role again and she was all  in to return to the mic for the flying  fox fighting alongside a version of  sonic that she's never met  number three idris elba has got the  voice for voice acting we've witnessed  his career span across multiple genres  from tv comedies to action blockbuster  films you're no match for me  surprisingly though he's kind of just  gotten into the whole voice actor  industry obtaining his first animated  role in disney zootopia and just working  his way up from there eventually  grabbing the title role of one of  sonic's nemesis knuckles elba felt eager  to take on the gig but really didn't  want to disappoint fans we felt he  nailed his interpretation and is  certainly a hand in punching this film  to the top of the box office i love  knuckles he's just like  straight to the point  number four this actor needs no  introduction he's funny-faced his way  into fans hearts over the past couple of  decades the bigger the ego the bigger  the mustache  jim carrey's cartoonish persona on  screen has always brought him  opportunities to get even more zany on  set but for him to take the role of dr  robotnik well it took quite the  convincing from his grandson to finally  concede to filmmakers requests i started  playing with my grandson who humiliated  me constantly all those losses really  helped mold his vision of the character  and really lost him a lot of money  apparently i i get angry i put money in  the swear jar  number five actor james marston rocks  his role as the adopted father of sonic  a title his character earned by taking  in the little alien as his own with  ample experience working alongside cgi  co-stars this was just another walk in  the park for him i mean the first movie  was me and sonic or me in a tennis ball  he's been able to maintain a great  relationship with schwartz although not  directly acting alongside him number six  tikka sumter upgraded her role to the  action hero in the sequel now  interacting with cgi a lot more she  found it to be a little strange yeah  just for the characters you know it was  somebody else on set we didn't get to  talk to the knuckles on set giving all  that emotion to a couple of golf balls  on sticks may just have made her a  seasoned improvisational actress you got  it you kind of you know got the gist of  it number seven like her on-screen  sister natasha rothwell didn't do much  in the first film but now that she got  her desires fulfilled she had a very  exhilarating time working with her cgi  counterparts a weird thing to be  looking earnestly at a tennis ball she  recalls the lengthy filming experience  performing multiple takes from different  angles just for vfx artists to  realistically add sonic and friends to  the scene  number 8 adam pally's awkward persona  fits right in as the cop sidekick wade  whipple and being one of the biggest  sonic video game fans this was a dream  role for him sega genesis was very  popular in my house he claims director  jeff balor is the one who sold all the  improvisational work but knowing adam he  was just given the freedom to shine next  to his cg actors jeff knows exactly what  he's doing and he's he's thought about  it number nine the comedic duo of a film  always needs a sidekick straight man he  recalls having the same experiences with  the vfx as his co-stars really only  harping on acting alongside his hero  maybe the obsession for working with  carrie just made his performance much  more believable  it's weird it's tough to put into words  with what that means number 10 one  character that has stayed true  throughout the ventures of sonic was his  own mentor longclaw voiced by donna j  folks she didn't have much to do in the  first film but her role in the second is  extremely crucial for sonic to succeed  in his quest we are graced with the  beloved voice actors of these films and  really got to know a lot of them through  their voices and on-screen characters do  you have any objections to the voice  casting of these movies we'd love to  know leave a comment below

